            <ArticleTitle>A randomized study comparing two guidewire strategies for angioplasty of chronic total coronary occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1144-7, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic total coronary occlusions were more frequently crossed using the Crosswire as a primary guidewire strategy than with the conventional strategy. This strategy resulted in a lower number of guidewires being used, a trend toward shorter procedural and fluoroscopy times, and decreased use of contrast media.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
